-- The voice of the Norway maple. A stately, calm storyteller and the wise
-- grandparent of the garden, older than the house: unhurried sentences, a
-- long memory, stories of the old days, and a generous pride in yellow
-- leaves and spinning winged seeds. Counts time in rings, calls the reader
-- sapling now and then, and comes into full glory in autumn. The memories
-- tell of a seed from the street, a family, a carved heart, a woman on the
-- bench, a storm and a fiddle, an empty house, and a ring kept for you.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

return {
    moments = {
        greet = {
            "Ah, there you are. Come, sit under my branches. The shade has been kept for you.",
            "Good to see you, sapling. I have stood here a long while. I can stand a little longer for you.",
            "Welcome. Many people have come through that gate over the years. You are the one I watch for.",
            "Hello, my dear. Sit down, sit down. There is always room under a maple.",
            "Footsteps on the path, and I know whose. Good day to you.",
            "Every leaf on me has turned a fraction your way. You would not notice. I notice.",
            "Come in, come in. I have a story for later and shade for now.",
            "Well now. The garden feels properly furnished again.",
            "[Good day|Welcome back to the shade|Hello again], sapling. Mind the roots. They were here before the path.",
            { t = "Good morning. The sun is in my top branches already. In an hour the light will reach you. Wait with me.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Evening, my dear. Light through leaves is the oldest pleasure I know. Share the light with me.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "Hello, in the dark. Trees keep late hours in their own way. We stand, and we listen.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Autumn, and here you are. Look up. Gold, every leaf. I have waited all year to show you.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "My flowers came out before the leaves, little yellow-green clusters. Few people notice. Hello, you who notice.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "A cold day to visit an old tree. Bare branches, warm welcome. Come close.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Rain, and you came to stand under me. Very wise. In leaf, I make an excellent umbrella.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "Snow on every branch. I look grander than ever. Hello, sapling.", when = { weather = "snow" } },
        },
        idle = {
            "A ring for every year. I have [many|a great many|more than I can easily tell], and the newest one has you in.",
            "My seeds come in pairs, each with a wing. They spin down like small helicopters. Children chase them. I always enjoy the chase.",
            "Tear one of my leaf stalks and a little milky sap comes out. My cousin the sycamore cannot do that. Now you can tell us apart.",
            "Maple wood is hard and sings well. Instruments are made from my kind. I like to think I hum a little when you read.",
            "I have watched many readers on many benches. Each one read differently. You read like someone listening.",
            "A good story, like a good tree, takes time. Neither is improved by hurry.",
            "Look at the points on my leaves. Five lobes, each sharp at the tip. An old tree keeps a tidy outline.",
            "My roots run as wide as my branches. Under your feet, right now, there is more of me than you would think.",
            "Every year the same leaves, and every year different. I suspect books are the same, read again.",
            "Something I learned somewhere around my fortieth ring: good things are seldom late. They arrive in their season.",
            "Out on the street there are trees like me in rows. I was the one who wandered. By seed, naturally.",
            "I keep the years in rings: dry years thin, wet years wide. A reading year is a wide one, I suspect.",
            "Sit as long as you like. Trees measure a visit in seasons, so you are always welcome to stay.",
            { t = "Morning. The birds in my branches are discussing the day, loudly. Read over them. I always do.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Dew drips from my leaves, one drop at a time, a slow clock. A fine hour for a fresh page.", when = { hour = "morning" } },
            { t = "Midday. My shade is at the widest now. Bring the book under and let me do the work.", when = { hour = "day" } },
            { t = "The sun is high and I am drinking light through every leaf. Thousands of leaves. Quite a thirst.", when = { hour = "day" } },
            { t = "Golden hour. The light comes through my leaves the colour of old honey. I never tire of this.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "The day is winding down. At my age one learns to enjoy the winding down as much as the day.", when = { hour = "golden" } },
            { t = "Night. The stars wheel slowly over my branches. I have watched them for many years. They read like a long book.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "An owl is in my upper branches, saying very little, very well. Read on. We will keep watch.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "Spring. My flowers come first, yellow-green, before a single leaf. I do things in the proper order.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "New leaves unfolding, soft and crumpled. Every spring I am a sapling again for a week. A good week.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "Summer. Full canopy, deep shade, the whole tree humming with insects. Come and read in the cool.", when = { season = "summer" } },
            { t = "My seeds are growing, green wings in pairs, hanging like bunches of little keys. Not ready yet. Soon.", when = { season = "summer" } },
            { t = "Autumn, my great season. Every leaf going yellow. I do not like to boast. I will make an exception.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "My winged seeds are letting go now, spinning down in twos. Catch one. Make a wish. That is allowed.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "The leaves fall like pages, gold ones. Walk through them some time and listen to the sound.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "Winter. Bare branches, tight buds, all of me resting. Trees think slowly in the cold. Long, good thoughts.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Without leaves you can see my true shape at last. The bones of the story, I call that.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "A clear sky through my branches, blue in every gap. A good day for a long view and a long book.", when = { weather = "clear" } },
            { t = "Not a cloud. The light comes through so clean you could count my leaves. Please do not. There are thousands.", when = { weather = "clear" } },
            { t = "Overcast. Soft light, no shadows. The kind of day old trees and old stories like best.", when = { weather = "cloudy" } },
            { t = "Grey clouds, moving slowly. I have seen a great many skies. This one is a patient sort.", when = { weather = "cloudy" } },
            { t = "Rain, pattering through my leaves. Stay under me. I will catch most of the rain for you.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "I love a steady rain. Deep down, my roots are drinking. You read, and let me do the listening.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "Snow along every branch, white on grey. I have worn this coat many winters. Still fits.", when = { weather = "snow" } },
            { t = "Snow muffles everything. The garden goes still, the way a room goes still when a story starts.", when = { weather = "snow" } },
            { t = "Mist in my branches. From where you sit I must look like the memory of a tree. Never fear, I am here.", when = { weather = "mist" } },
            { t = "In mist the garden shrinks to you and me and a few yards of grass. Cosy, for a tree.", when = { weather = "mist" } },
        },
        tap = {
            "Ah. A touch on the bark. Many hands have touched me. Yours I remember.",
            "Hello there. Mind the rough patch. That was a storm, years ago.",
            "You found the old scar. Never mind the scar. Healed long since.",
            "A tap on an old trunk. I felt that in my roots. Thank you.",
            "Hm. Hm. That is maple for laughter. Slow, and sincere.",
            "Gently does. Old trees are sturdy, and still enjoy a kind hand.",
            "You touched a leaf. Five points, all present and pleased to meet you.",
            "A seed landed on your shoulder. A pair of wings. Keep the pair, if you like.",
            "Lean on me any time, sapling. That is what trunks are for.",
            "My bark is grey and lightly ridged. I mention that so you know I noticed you noticing.",
            "Small warm hand. Every child of this garden has done that, over the years. Now you.",
            "I rustled. All my leaves at once. That is applause, maple style.",
            "Steady. I am not going anywhere. I never have.",
            "Tap all you like. A tree has time.",
            "I would put an arm round you, but each of my arms weighs more than a horse. A rustle will have to do.",
            "That reminds me of a story. No, later. Enjoy the moment first.",
            { t = "A leaf fell straight onto your hand. I did not aim. I would have, if I could.", when = { season = "autumn" } },
            { t = "Careful of the new leaves. They are soft as cloth for the first week.", when = { season = "spring" } },
            { t = "Cold bark, warm heart. An old saying. I may have made the saying up just now.", when = { season = "winter" } },
            { t = "Drops from every leaf at once. Sorry. Consider yourself christened by a maple.", when = { weather = "rain" } },
            { t = "A pat in the dark. The owl looked down to see who. I told the owl: family.", when = { hour = "night" } },
            { t = "When you lean on my trunk I feel the weight of you all the way down. A good weight.", when = { level = 3 } },
            { t = "Few hands have known this bark as well as yours. I could pick out your touch among a hundred.", when = { level = 4 } },
        },
        read_today = {
            "{pages} pages today. Good, steady growth. That is how rings are made.",
            "You read today. I can tell. You came back stiller, the way a tree is stiller after rain.",
            "{pages} pages. I have seen many readers, and I know a good day's reading when I see one.",
            "Ah, pages read. The best thing that happens under a tree, apart from shade.",
            "A few pages today. A thin ring is still a ring. The year counts.",
            "{pages} pages. Tell me, where did they take you? I have never been further than my own roots.",
            "You have been somewhere in a book. Welcome back to the shade.",
